return Convert.ToHexString(bytes);

`async void` makes exceptions unobservable and crashes the process, and callers can't await completion. The reader is never disposed. `Parallel.ForEach` mutates a non-thread-safe static `Dictionary` concurrently, which corrupts data or throws. Return `Task`, dispose the reader, and guard the shared state with a lock.

Improved code:
private static readonly object Gate = new();

public async Task ImportAsync(string csvPath)
{
    using var reader = new StreamReader(csvPath);
    var lines = new List<string>();
    string? line;
    while ((line = await reader.ReadLineAsync()) != null)
    {
        lines.Add(line);
    }

    Parallel.ForEach(lines.Skip(1), row =>
    {
        var cols = row.Split(',');
        var customer = cols[1];
        var total = decimal.Parse(cols[2]) * rates.ToUsd(cols[3]);
        lock (Gate)
        {
            TotalsByCustomer[customer] = TotalsByCustomer.GetValueOrDefault(customer) + total;
        }
    });
}

`name` is concatenated into a shell command, so input like `x; rm -rf ~` runs arbitrary commands. Pass arguments with `execFileSync` so no shell is involved. Also restrict `name` to a safe character set to block option injection and path traversal.

Improved code:
import { execFileSync } from "node:child_process";

export function exportReport(name: string): Buffer {
  if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(name)) {
    throw new Error("Invalid report name");
  }
  return execFileSync("pdf-render", ["--out", "/tmp/reports", `${name}.pdf`]);
}

Calling `eval` on a user-supplied `formula` lets callers execute arbitrary JavaScript. Allow only numeric literals, arithmetic operators, parentheses and whitespace. Then evaluate in an isolated `Function` with strict mode, or use a dedicated expression parser.

Improved code:
export function evaluate(formula: string): number {
  if (!/^[0-9+\-*/%().\s]+$/.test(formula)) {
    throw new Error("Invalid formula");
  }
  return Number(new Function(`"use strict"; return (${formula});`)());
}

A live payments API token is hardcoded in source, which exposes it to anyone with repository access. Load it from the environment and fail fast if it is missing. The leaked token should also be rotated.

Improved code:
const paymentsToken = process.env.PAYMENTS_API_TOKEN;
if (!paymentsToken) {
  throw new Error("PAYMENTS_API_TOKEN is not set");
}
export const PAYMENTS_API_TOKEN: string = paymentsToken;

`eval` on an arbitrary string allows arbitrary code execution. Replace it with a safe expression parser, or at minimum validate the input against a strict whitelist of arithmetic characters before evaluating.

Improved code:
if (!/^[0-9+\-*/().\s]+$/.test(formula)) {
  throw new Error("Invalid formula");
}
return Number(new Function(`"use strict"; return (${formula});`)());

Concatenating `name` into a shell command string allows command injection. Use `execFileSync` with an argument array, which bypasses the shell, and validate `name` to block path traversal.

Improved code:
if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(name)) {
  throw new Error("Invalid report name");
}
return execFileSync("pdf-render", ["--out", "/tmp/reports", name + ".pdf"]);

