The cleanup lambda is registered before `uv_os_environ` initializes `items` and `count`. If the CHECK fails, or any code runs in between, cleanup would use uninitialized values. Initialize the variables and register cleanup only after a successful call.

Improved code:
MaybeLocal<Array> RealEnvStore::Pairs(Isolate* isolate) const {
  Mutex::ScopedLock lock(per_process::env_var_mutex);
  uv_env_item_t* items = nullptr;
  int count = 0;

  CHECK_EQ(uv_os_environ(&items, &count), 0);
  auto cleanup = OnScopeLeave([&]() { uv_os_free_environ(items, count); });

